1
00:00:00,275 --> 00:00:03,785
Watching videos feels productive,
until you try solving alone.

2
00:00:04,294 --> 00:00:10,227
Blitz Learning is our engineering prototype
turning passive video watching into active math practice.

3
00:00:10,817 --> 00:00:15,980
On our neutral front door, future subjects say coming soon
while math is playable now.

4
00:00:16,366 --> 00:00:18,794
Learners pick a math quest, a problem,

5
00:00:18,985 --> 00:00:21,131
and an original nonhuman tutor:

6
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:23,754
a robot, fox, or fantasy creature.

7
00:00:24,125 --> 00:00:28,979
These real captured screens show controlled local practice,
not live AI.

8
00:00:29,372 --> 00:00:32,864
An offline deterministic checker
grades numeric answers:

9
00:00:33,198 --> 00:00:36,028
one to three consecutive correct fresh questions

10
00:00:36,317 --> 00:00:40,513
earn one to three stars, and errors reset streaks,
not best stars.

11
00:00:41,109 --> 00:00:50,244
Next, our architecture pairs Gemini 4 Argon for explanations
with Gemini Live for optional voice discussion and consented written work photos.

12
00:00:50,803 --> 00:00:57,613
Our roadmap adds more subjects, outcome evaluation, privacy hardening,
and explicit check ins, never facial tracking.
